{:id "0058-lab-flick-ui"
 :title "Lab flick, the page: 'Which?' reads your line back two ways and your style moves toward the one you pick"
 :lupa/deps #{"0053-lab-flick" "0059-lab-flick-turn"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md, 'How people and agents drive it', and the
        H5 result in docs/product/lab-notebook.md. The pure exam is
        lab.flick (order 0053). Put it on the page: on request the lab
        reads the current line back as A (your style now) and as B (one
        step along one axis), you flick toward the one you like, and your
        style point moves. Never unprompted."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc"
         "test/halfahead/lab/debug_test.cljc" "public/lab/index.html"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "lab.main and index.html: a 'Which?' button in the bar and Ctrl+/
            start an exam on the current text (disabled with no text or
            with reduced motion; if offer gives nil the chip says 'Nothing
            more to tell apart on this line' for two seconds and nothing
            else happens: that is how an exam ends, order 0059). During it: a chip
            reads 'A' while A plays, 'B' while B plays, then 'A  or  B ?'
            with two buttons; the left and right arrow keys, or the
            buttons, choose; Escape cancels and changes nothing; R plays
            the pair again. Each reading plays through the lab's reading
            path with the pair's point as the style (dress included). On
            a choice the learn state is (flick/decide ...), the style
            becomes Mine at the state's point (the board's XY dot moves
            with it), and the state is remembered per viewer in
            localStorage (try/catch). The chip is an aria-live region so
            a screen reader hears 'A', 'B', 'A or B?'. The picker's choice
            is remembered per viewer as well (today only the point is, so
            a reload falls back to Auto and a learned style is not in
            force): a reload starts in the style last picked, Mine
            included (existing browser checks that count on Auto at the
            start must still pass: give them a fresh page with empty
            storage where they need one). window.__lab.flick()
            -> {phase axis pointA pointB flicks point} as plain data. The
            debug overlay shows 'flick 3 · asking energy · step 0.25'.
          Tests: the debug line for a flick.
          e2e/lab.mjs, a new step 'flick' (?debug&reveal=3): type 'I
          loooove this (honestly). But maybe not. Ship it!' and wait for
          rest; Ctrl+/: flick().phase goes a, then b, then choose (wait on
          the data, not on the clock), and the two readings ran with
          different points (pointA and pointB differ on exactly the axis
          reported); press ArrowRight: flick().flicks is 1, point equals
          pointB, and the style picker shows Mine; Ctrl+/ then Escape:
          nothing changes; four more exams always choosing the option with
          the higher energy: point.energy has not fallen; reload: the
          point and the flick count are kept and the picker still shows
          Mine; pick Elegant and reload: the picker shows Elegant. Screenshot out/lab/flick.png
          during the choose phase.
          docs/LAB.md: a short section 'The flick'. Its lesson, from the
          H5 simulation: a careful chooser's point closes on their taste
          (distance 0.292 to 0.067 in 12 flicks), a chooser who is wrong
          one time in four does not converge, so the two readings must be
          easy to tell apart and the axes few."
 :acceptance
 ["debug tests as in the design, on both hosts; `bb test` stays green"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the flick step and every existing step;
   out/lab/flick.png for the foreman"]
 :non-goals
 ["Never start an exam unprompted; no telemetry; nothing leaves the device"
  "No change to lab.flick, lab.learn, reading, pace, marks, score,
   gestures, synth, dress, the board's pads, the renderer or the
   director; do not edit the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/lab/flick.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/board.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "src/halfahead/lab/debug.cljc"
           "public/lab/index.html" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
